WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.601
-Welcome back to the show.
-So good to be here.

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:03.934
-I want to talk about
"Barbarian."

00:00:03.934 --> 00:00:05.300
But I have lots of things
to talk to you about.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.667
First of all, I saw you
yesterday with Drew Barrymore.

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:10.200
-Yes.
-On her show.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.334
And I thought that was
fantastic.

00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:14.534
-It was so nice to see her.
It was so good to --

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:16.501
It was wild to do that
in front of --

00:00:16.501 --> 00:00:19.133
You know, to reconnect
in front of strangers on TV.

00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:20.634
-In front of America.

00:00:20.634 --> 00:00:22.901
You met -- unbelievable --
another celebrity backstage.

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:24.634
-Yes.
-This is why I was laughing

00:00:24.634 --> 00:00:27.033
when we were playing this game,
the last one,

00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:30.767
you met the cornbassador
of South Dakota.

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:33.400
-Tariq.
He was so -- Yes.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.868
-This kid is unbelievable.
-Yeah.

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:37.767
He was so cute, obviously.

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:40.467
Oh, big surprise -- he was cute.
-Yeah.

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:42.534
Big surprise --
he really was cute.

00:00:42.534 --> 00:00:45.133
-It wasn't an act.
But I said to him, because,

00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:47.901
obviously, he loves --
we all know he loves corn.

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:49.901
But I said,
"What are some of the things

00:00:49.901 --> 00:00:52.100
you don't really like?
What are you not crazy about?"

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.467
-[ Gasps ]
This is an exclusive?

00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:55.300
-This is a big scoop, guys.
So --

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.334
-This is gonna be all over
...tomorrow.

00:00:57.334 --> 00:01:01.334
-Yeah, so I can report
that Tariq does not like

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:05.234
strawberries or peaches
or -- sorry to say --

00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:07.701
"Sonic the Hedgehog 2," but he
loves "Alvin and the Chipmunks."

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:08.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:12.234
So, he prefers a chipmunk
to a hedgehog.

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:15.767
Sorry, Ben Schwartz and everyone
in "Sonic the Hedgehog."

00:01:15.767 --> 00:01:17.801
-I wanted to ask you,
while I had you here,

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:19.400
'cause I know
you're a great actor,

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.801
but you're also very good
at doing impressions.

00:01:21.801 --> 00:01:23.868
We've always done them
to each other backstage.

00:01:23.868 --> 00:01:25.901
-Yeah, people love it.
People around us are...

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:27.767
-I hope people love it.
-...not at all annoyed by our...

00:01:27.767 --> 00:01:30.801
-No. Here's you.
This is in --

00:01:30.801 --> 00:01:32.868
This is in "Walk Hard:
The Dewey Cox Story."

00:01:32.868 --> 00:01:34.334
-Oh, yeah.
Yeah.

00:01:34.334 --> 00:01:35.701
-And you were George Harrison.

00:01:35.701 --> 00:01:37.033
-Oh, man.
It was a thrill.

00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:40.234
-With Paul Rudd,
Jason Schwartzman, Jack Black.

00:01:40.234 --> 00:01:42.033
-And the great --
-John C. Reilly.

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:45.200
-I mean, these are all
my favorite -- not myself.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.300
All my --
some of my favorite performers.

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.501
And so I got this call --

00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:50.667
-Were you nervous
to play with the Beatles?

00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:52.501
-I was because it was --

00:01:52.501 --> 00:01:54.501
You know,
the stakes couldn't be higher.

00:01:54.501 --> 00:01:56.033
It's the Beatles.

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:58.133
If you like music,
you love the Beatles.

00:01:58.133 --> 00:02:01.200
And I grew up listening --
you know, we both --

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.734
Everyone loves the Beatles.
I don't have to make that point.

00:02:03.734 --> 00:02:05.567
So, I got --
-Judd called you?

00:02:05.567 --> 00:02:08.601
-Judd called and said, "I want
you to play George Harrison."

00:02:08.601 --> 00:02:10.801
And I of course said yes.

00:02:10.801 --> 00:02:12.133
And, um,
we had a day to prepare.

00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:14.801
And so I called Paul Rudd,
who --

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:17.234
It's a very name-droppy story,
but you mentioned him, also.

00:02:17.234 --> 00:02:18.400
Paul was playing John Lennon.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.801
And I said,
"Paul, you know, I'm nervous.

00:02:20.801 --> 00:02:21.834
We're playing the Beatles."

00:02:21.834 --> 00:02:23.200
And he's like,
"Dude, I'm nervous, too.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.467
I know, we only have a day."

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:26.167
And so I went over
to his hotel room.

00:02:26.167 --> 00:02:28.701
And we just watched
as much footage as we could

00:02:28.701 --> 00:02:30.901
of the Beatles
in interviews and stuff.

00:02:30.901 --> 00:02:33.367
And while we were there,
Jason Schwartzman called.

00:02:33.367 --> 00:02:34.601
He was playing Ringo.
And he said,

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:36.367
"Dude, I'm so nervous.
Are you guys nervous?"

00:02:36.367 --> 00:02:38.300
And so, the three of us were,

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.367
you know, sharing our nerves
with each other.

00:02:40.367 --> 00:02:43.234
And as we were watching them,

00:02:43.234 --> 00:02:47.000
I never really realized
how distinct they all were.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.868
You do such a great --
-How does Paul go?

00:02:49.868 --> 00:02:53.334
-Well, Paul -- Paul's very --
you know, with him, it's --

00:02:53.334 --> 00:02:56.033
I like to, like,
hook into something.

00:02:56.033 --> 00:02:57.901
Like, if it's a word
or just sort of a look.

00:02:57.901 --> 00:03:01.701
And he's got his eyebrow
always kind of up like this.

00:03:01.701 --> 00:03:03.734
And it's very sing songy,
you know?

00:03:03.734 --> 00:03:05.834
And he says, "you know," a lot.
You know, up and down.

00:03:05.834 --> 00:03:07.434
-Yeah, you know, yeah.

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:09.834
-It's sort of like this.
-We're the Beatles, you know.

00:03:09.834 --> 00:03:10.934
Yeah.
-And we're doing this.

00:03:10.934 --> 00:03:12.868
-That's good.
-And then, John is --

00:03:12.868 --> 00:03:14.968
There's something kind of
nasally about John.

00:03:14.968 --> 00:03:17.267
You know, John's very --

00:03:17.267 --> 00:03:19.300
It's all kind of directed
through the nose there.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:22.067
-Yeah, he's very nasally.
Speaking only through his nose.

00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:24.467
-Sort of like that, yes.
And Ringo, you have to --

00:03:24.467 --> 00:03:26.267
It's the least flattering --
the most unflattering.

00:03:26.267 --> 00:03:28.067
You kind of have to put
your head back like this.

00:03:28.067 --> 00:03:30.000
And Ringo kind of acts
like this.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.067
But I thought, "George --
What is George's hook?"

00:03:32.067 --> 00:03:34.767
And I realized it was just --

00:03:34.767 --> 00:03:38.567
He's just -- He's just
so contemplative, you know?

00:03:38.567 --> 00:03:40.501
And everything
is sort of like this.

00:03:40.501 --> 00:03:42.367
And, of course,
I was sad when John died.

00:03:42.367 --> 00:03:44.267
But it was -- you know,
I knew -- I knew --

00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:46.167
I was sad because I'd never
play guitar with him again.

00:03:46.167 --> 00:03:49.701
-Wow, wow, wow!
That is good!

00:03:49.701 --> 00:03:51.934
You can do all the Beatles!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:51.934 --> 00:03:54.200
-So, then, were like --
So at the end of this --

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.834
at the end of this, you know,
session with Paul,

00:03:56.834 --> 00:04:00.167
I'm leaving Paul Rudd,
I'm leaving his hotel room,

00:04:00.167 --> 00:04:01.667
and he said -- you know,
I shouldn't tell you --

00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:03.167
I said, "I wonder
how Jack Black's feeling."

00:04:03.167 --> 00:04:04.634
You know, 'cause Jack's
gotta play Paul McCartney.

00:04:04.634 --> 00:04:07.100
And Paul said,
"I shouldn't tell you this,

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:09.067
but I ran into Jack
the other day,

00:04:09.067 --> 00:04:10.100
and I asked him that.

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:11.400
I said,
'Dude, aren't you nervous?

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:12.701
We're playing the Beatles.'

00:04:12.701 --> 00:04:14.133
And he said,
"No, dude, I got it.

00:04:14.133 --> 00:04:15.868
It's in the bag."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.868 --> 00:04:18.234
And Paul goes,
"How did you do --"

00:04:18.234 --> 00:04:20.300
He goes, "Dude,
just watch 'Hard Day's Night.'

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.534
That's all you gotta do
is watch 'Hard Day's Night.'"

00:04:22.534 --> 00:04:24.834
So, we were like,
"Oh [bleep] no."

00:04:24.834 --> 00:04:26.067
-Dude.
-Dude.

00:04:26.067 --> 00:04:27.801
Dude, it's in the bag.
-Dude, it's in the bag.

00:04:27.801 --> 00:04:30.400
-I got it, dude.
I [bleep] got it, dude.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:31.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.868 --> 00:04:33.601
And so, were like,
"Oh, Jack's gonna

00:04:33.601 --> 00:04:35.334
blow us all out of the water.
-Yeah, of course he is.

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:36.701
-And so we show up on set.

00:04:36.701 --> 00:04:38.667
And Jack's got the first line
in rehearsal.

00:04:38.667 --> 00:04:40.901
And he goes --
he's got the outfit on.

00:04:40.901 --> 00:04:42.234
He's doing the eyebrows.

00:04:42.234 --> 00:04:43.434
You know,
he's got that kind of going.

00:04:43.434 --> 00:04:45.067
And he goes --
he's right here, and he goes,

00:04:45.067 --> 00:04:47.167
[ Scottish accent ]
"I'm Paul McCartney, eh?

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:49.234
[ Laughter ]
Like, full-on Scottish.

00:04:49.234 --> 00:04:50.467
And I looked at Rudd,
and we're like,

00:04:50.467 --> 00:04:53.167
"What's going on?"
And -- but --

00:04:53.167 --> 00:04:54.934
But the lesson that we learned,

00:04:54.934 --> 00:04:56.133
which we shouldn't
have needed to learn,

00:04:56.133 --> 00:04:58.667
is that Jack
still stole the show

00:04:58.667 --> 00:05:00.501
because he's [bleep] Jack Black,

00:05:00.501 --> 00:05:01.634
and he's the greatest
of all time.

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:03.167
-Yeah, of course.
Don't worry.

00:05:03.167 --> 00:05:04.667
Don't overthink it.
-Yes, exactly.

00:05:04.667 --> 00:05:06.300
We were overthinking it.
And he was just --

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.200
He's like, "Everyone knows
I'm not Paul McCartney.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.234
I'm Jack Black."
And it was so funny.

00:05:10.234 --> 00:05:11.601
It was so good.
He was brilliant.

00:05:11.601 --> 00:05:13.701
-I love Jack Black.
-I love Jack Black.

00:05:13.701 --> 00:05:17.200
Everyone loves Jack Black.
-He could do that.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:19.801
Let's talk about the --
you're in the number-one movie

00:05:19.801 --> 00:05:21.868
right now in the country,
"Barbarian."

00:05:21.868 --> 00:05:23.634
Congratulations on this.
-Thanks, man.

00:05:23.634 --> 00:05:24.868
-Frightening.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:24.868 --> 00:05:28.133
-So fun.
It's fun.

00:05:28.133 --> 00:05:30.367
-Scary movies
getting great reviews.

00:05:30.367 --> 00:05:31.567
How did you feel
when you found out

00:05:31.567 --> 00:05:33.501
it was the number-one movie
in the country?

00:05:33.501 --> 00:05:34.968
-It was exciting.
I got a text --

00:05:34.968 --> 00:05:38.100
I was in my place, which you've
been to up in Massachusetts.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:40.434
I live in kind of
a rural area up there.

00:05:40.434 --> 00:05:43.901
And all of my neighbors
are over 70.

00:05:43.901 --> 00:05:45.601
And I got this text
from the director, Zach Cregger,

00:05:45.601 --> 00:05:46.968
who's brilliant, and he said,

00:05:46.968 --> 00:05:48.701
"Hey, we got
the number-one movie."

00:05:48.701 --> 00:05:51.501
And I said -- I said it to them.
I was proud.

00:05:51.501 --> 00:05:53.067
I had a moment where I said,
"Hey, you guys,

00:05:53.067 --> 00:05:55.801
I'm in the number-one movie."

00:05:55.801 --> 00:05:57.834
And they said, "Oh, yeah?
What's it called?"

00:05:57.834 --> 00:06:00.534
I said, "It's 'Barbarian.'"
And he said, "Oh, okay."

00:06:00.534 --> 00:06:02.434
And one of them said,
"Hey, by the way,

00:06:02.434 --> 00:06:05.467
why aren't you ever
watering your garden?"

00:06:05.467 --> 00:06:07.801
And I said,
"Uh, what do you mean?"

00:06:07.801 --> 00:06:10.167
He goes, "You're never here.
You're never here.

00:06:10.167 --> 00:06:11.467
And Mick's
having to water your garden."

00:06:11.467 --> 00:06:13.167
-They could care less.
-Care less.

00:06:13.167 --> 00:06:14.801
-They can care less
about this movie.

00:06:14.801 --> 00:06:16.334
-And I said, "Well, I've been
promoting this movie."

00:06:16.334 --> 00:06:17.467
He goes, "Promoting?

00:06:17.467 --> 00:06:18.501
What do you have
to do that for?"

00:06:18.501 --> 00:06:19.734
He says,
"You gotta water the garden."

00:06:19.734 --> 00:06:21.167
[ Laughter ]
And as I was leaving,

00:06:21.167 --> 00:06:22.267
I said to Mick -- I said,

00:06:22.267 --> 00:06:23.400
"So, are you gonna
go see 'Barbarian'?"

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:24.667
He goes, "Oh, yeah.

00:06:24.667 --> 00:06:26.067
I'm gonna go
to the local multiplex,"

00:06:26.067 --> 00:06:27.534
the joke being
there's no movie theater

00:06:27.534 --> 00:06:29.033
anywhere near where I live.

00:06:29.033 --> 00:06:31.100
So, they're not gonna watch it.
-They're not gonna watch it?

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:32.701
That's a good
humble pie there for you.

00:06:32.701 --> 00:06:34.767
-It was.
It was -- everything's relative.

00:06:34.767 --> 00:06:36.701
-I love Zach Cregger,
by the way.

00:06:36.701 --> 00:06:38.100
He's great.
He wrote and directed this.

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:39.400
-Yes.
-He's talented.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:40.901
-From The Whitest Kids You Know,
the sketch comedy group.

00:06:40.901 --> 00:06:42.467
-Talented guy.
-Really brilliant.

00:06:42.467 --> 00:06:44.267
-But it's frightening.
-It is.

00:06:44.267 --> 00:06:45.734
It's scary.
It's wild.

00:06:45.734 --> 00:06:47.334
And there's some turns.
And it's one of those movies

00:06:47.334 --> 00:06:50.200
that we're supposed to be
talking about it,

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:52.400
but we're not supposed
to say anything about it.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:54.100
So it's a little challenging.

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:56.133
-Yeah, well, I guess that's the
fun part of these scary movies.

00:06:56.133 --> 00:06:57.701
Because you're like,
"Well, don't spoil it."

00:06:57.701 --> 00:07:00.133
Because every single thing
could be possibly a spoiler.

00:07:00.133 --> 00:07:01.567
-Totally.
And it is.

00:07:01.567 --> 00:07:05.067
It really is.
The twists and turns are wild.

00:07:05.067 --> 00:07:06.167
They're fun.
-Well, we could say

00:07:06.167 --> 00:07:07.868
someone moves into a --
rents a house.

00:07:07.868 --> 00:07:09.300
-No.
No.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:10.601
Don't say --
Yeah, we can say --

00:07:10.601 --> 00:07:11.767
Sorry, sorry.

00:07:11.767 --> 00:07:13.067
We can say
there are people in it.

00:07:13.067 --> 00:07:14.367
-Okay.
-No, no.

00:07:14.367 --> 00:07:16.434
Yeah, someone rents a house.
Someone rents a house.

00:07:16.434 --> 00:07:17.901
-An Airbnb.
Yeah, it's an Airbnb.

00:07:17.901 --> 00:07:19.734
That'll sell it.
Someone rents a house.

00:07:19.734 --> 00:07:21.868
-Yeah.
That's a great story.

00:07:21.868 --> 00:07:23.834
Someone rents an Airbnb.
-No, sorry, Jim.

00:07:23.834 --> 00:07:25.467
Wait, sorry.
They rent a house,

00:07:25.467 --> 00:07:27.801
and it gets double-booked.
So, Bill Skarsgard

00:07:27.801 --> 00:07:30.067
and Georgina Campbell,
who are so good, they --

00:07:30.067 --> 00:07:32.434
they find themselves together
in this --

00:07:32.434 --> 00:07:35.534
Not an Airbnb,
it's a scare-bnb.

00:07:35.534 --> 00:07:37.434
-Ooh-ooh-ooh-ooh!
-Ooh-ooh-ooh-ooh! Yes!

00:07:37.434 --> 00:07:38.567
-Is there anything you learned

00:07:38.567 --> 00:07:40.334
from making this film
for the future?

00:07:40.334 --> 00:07:43.767
Anything you're like, "Oh."
-I would just say I love Airbnb.

00:07:43.767 --> 00:07:45.334
It's a great company.
They do a lot of

00:07:45.334 --> 00:07:47.133
great work with --
-Yeah, yeah, of course.

00:07:47.133 --> 00:07:50.734
-But I would say,
check the basement.

00:07:50.734 --> 00:07:52.567
That's what I'm gonna do
from now on.

00:07:52.567 --> 00:07:54.300
Wink.

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:55.634
-That's all you gotta say
right there.

00:07:55.634 --> 00:07:58.400
That is the best way
you could ever sell this movie.

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:00.167
-Yeah.
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:08:00.167 --> 00:08:02.100
Here's Justin Long
in "Barbarian."

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:05.601
Take a look at this.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:05.601 --> 00:08:07.601
-Hello?

00:08:24.234 --> 00:08:29.467
-I like to let my baby determine
how long he likes to nurse.

00:08:29.467 --> 00:08:32.200
-Oh, God.

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:34.200
[ Tape measure unspooling ]

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:39.067
[ Tense music plays ]

00:08:40.601 --> 00:08:43.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:45.000
-Justin Long!

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:47.100
"Barbarian" is in theaters
right now.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:48.801
Ellie Goulding performs for us
after the break.

00:08:48.801 --> 00:08:50.300
Stick around, everybody.

